# Build output — regenerated by `twsix build`, published by Actions.
site/

# Never commit the source workbook: it is the user's file, it is 6 MB, and
# everything the project needs from it is already frozen in tests/golden/.
*.xlsm
*.xlsx

# `twsix fetch-stock` output stays TRACKED, and the reason is worth writing
# down because it was ignored for about an hour on the opposite reasoning.
#
# The argument for ignoring it was "nothing depends on it — the tests read the
# frozen samples in tests/pages/".  True of the tests, false of the site:
# `twsix build` renders the ten-section page for exactly those stocks whose
# sheets are on disk, so this directory *is* the watchlist.  Ignoring it meant
# CI had nothing to build from and every stock got the thin grade table.
#
# It is a cache and it does go stale — that is what the 資料截止 line on every
# page is for.
